[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186189892 :answer-field/choices 17592186189893] [:db/retract 17592186189892 :answer-field/choices 17592186189894] [:db/retract 17592186189892 :answer-field/choices 17592186189895] [:db/retract 17592186189892 :answer-field/choices 17592186189896] [:db/retract 17592186189892 :answer-field/choices 17592186189897] [:db/retract 17592186189964 :answer-field/choices 17592186189968] [:db/retract 17592186189964 :answer-field/choices 17592186189969] [:db/retract 17592186189964 :answer-field/choices 17592186189965] [:db/retract 17592186189964 :answer-field/choices 17592186189966] [:db/retract 17592186189964 :answer-field/choices 17592186189967] {:db/id 17592186192697 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f2fd8190-fb82-5675-b05f-057d697af7cd" "question-1883917d-29b4-5836-94bf-f6ba9fe053f5" "question-f867e6a6-dbb2-59f4-99c3-23f6d9793b91" "question-11b34dc5-01d5-59cc-afad-bce1d288e367" "question-aa587d06-3d76-54dc-bc14-c7a25e414d3a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192402 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = 1 - \\dfrac{1}{3}\\sqrt{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = 1 - \\dfrac{1}{3}\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = 1 - \\dfrac{1}{3}\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{y} & =1-x \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & =3(1-x) \\\\ (\\sqrt{y})^{2} & ={(3(1-x))}^{2} \\\\ y & =9(1-x)^{2} \\\\ y & =9(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = 9(x - 1)^2.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx \\geq 0, \\qquad f(x) \\leq 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of $f^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx \\leq 1, \\qquad f^{-1}(x) \\geq 0.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192707 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f93430f2-f761-5264-8e7c-28207f8a2873" "question-3c4a5911-5181-51eb-9128-55f7bf7227a5" "question-0b14029b-c258-5cb1-9467-400506e4dea8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192415 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function ![](images/b9/b9a5eece426fa2aa66aac43b9afaf2812dcf483795a84d5e96fa89c0dcd71db6.svg)" :question/worked-solution "To find ![](images/6e/6e9ea2da83f324dd20158e4b08fb1c6968b6387d458964f21ed03648be954752.svg) we start by replacing ![](images/93/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) with ![](images/02/028bcadf67e469d96df97e89362f88bb8edca3ddea5579906987cc124663fba8.svg)\n![](images/d4/d4f5098eaa3eb85b97ec9547373f138922d22d734018ede816930c665248c0d5.svg)\n\nNow, interchanging ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) and ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) gives\n![](images/35/35c51b7dff42eeb3c3b2033c78495c07294048ba02628e583382c0807e43d192.svg)\n\nThen, we make ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) the subject of the equation, as follows:\n![](images/18/183e560a55c159a77b1ceacec766572e2279ad4e552242d638a9fdcf96f2c859.svg)\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n![](images/b5/b55f51d46d8917e5a44e4dae697c71a004580924cecd5a5f079e5eac7f480b3a.svg)\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of ![](images/93/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) are\n![](images/f2/f2f23ba499fcbb1dee1964f08453be99bdf5ed7ec11581b773845c4aa307b64a.svg)\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of ![](images/90/90bf8beda1404c3f6e9d9d9565922945fb59df9b0488050e3d2b72a153addd3c.svg) are\n![](images/96/96d9c5432e8f14ac6d9bc1841e37772cad060e3d09065129f73161726aeeffd2.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192698 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-37674798-c6eb-521f-b1bd-86df515c51cc" "question-14c0067f-8b9b-586e-a9fe-ecef26e510a6" "question-286413cf-e05b-52a9-9010-9fd10625bdfe" "question-f36e5ef3-ccb2-5795-aca3-91dfb93e14f0" "question-7e395659-7f2e-5dda-a6c4-f51ac9defcd5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192403 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{5}\\sqrt{4x + 1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{5}\\sqrt{4x + 1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{1}{5}\\sqrt{4y + 1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{4y+1} \\\\ \\sqrt{4y+1} & =5x \\\\ {(\\sqrt{4y+1})}^{2} & ={(5x)}^{2} \\\\ 4y+1 & =25{x}^{2} \\\\ 4y & =25{x}^{2}-1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{4}(25{x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\left(25x^2 - 1\\right).\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are given by\n\n$$\nx \\geq -\\dfrac14, \\qquad f(x) \\geq 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of $f^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx \\geq 0, \\qquad f^{-1}(x) \\geq -\\dfrac14.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192699 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5cb5bb60-d097-50b4-9ba5-bde88e86a4d3" "question-22e0c565-a427-5cb0-889a-a9c4e5867def" "question-635cbae5-da30-5f6f-818b-8857829587ba" "question-082ab1b4-7b0d-5301-97bc-d24a513a580b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192404 :question/problem "The function $f(x) = 3\\sqrt{x + k} - 2$ has an inverse function given by $f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{1}{9}(x + 2)^2 + 3.$ What is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = 3\\sqrt{x+k} - 2\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = 3\\sqrt{y + k} - 2.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\sqrt{y+k}-2 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{y+k} & =x+2 \\\\ \\sqrt{y+k} & =\\frac{1}{3}(x+2) \\\\ {(\\sqrt{y+k})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{3}(x+2))}^{2} \\\\ y+k & =\\frac{1}{9}(x+2)^{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{9}(x+2)^{2}-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{1}{9}(x + 2)^2 - k.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-k = 3 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad k = -3.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are given by\n\n$$\nx \\geq 3, \\qquad f(x) \\geq -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of $f^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx \\geq -2, \\qquad f^{-1}(x) \\geq3.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f2fd8190-fb82-5675-b05f-057d697af7cd" :question/id #uuid "f2fd8190-fb82-5675-b05f-057d697af7cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-270776" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{x}-10.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{x}-10\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{y}-10.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{y}-10 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{y} & =x+10 \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & =\\frac{3}{2}(x+10) \\\\ (\\sqrt{y})^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2}(x+10))}^{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{4}(x+10)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{9}{4}(x+10)^{2}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx\\ge 0,\\,f(x)\\ge -10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx\\ge -10,\\,{f}^{-1}(x)\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-87121302-8c37-5665-97c7-f22db0a986f9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-87121302-8c37-5665-97c7-f22db0a986f9" :answer-field/id #uuid "87121302-8c37-5665-97c7-f22db0a986f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8ca68a00-32fb-52b6-9611-af784188ac51" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ca68a00-32fb-52b6-9611-af784188ac51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ca68a00-32fb-52b6-9611-af784188ac51" :answer/id #uuid "8ca68a00-32fb-52b6-9611-af784188ac51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}(x+10)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1883917d-29b4-5836-94bf-f6ba9fe053f5" :question/id #uuid "1883917d-29b4-5836-94bf-f6ba9fe053f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-277054" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=5\\sqrt[3]{x}+3.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=5\\sqrt[3]{x}+3\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=5\\sqrt[3]{y}+3.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\sqrt[3]{y}+3 \\\\ 5\\sqrt[3]{y} & =x-3 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =\\frac{1}{5}(x-3) \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{y})^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{5}(x-3))}^{3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{125}(x-3)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{125}(x-3)^{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-77ca7a05-762c-5491-b3c2-14aaeb97dc53"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-77ca7a05-762c-5491-b3c2-14aaeb97dc53" :answer-field/id #uuid "77ca7a05-762c-5491-b3c2-14aaeb97dc53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-760022a2-75fb-5225-a136-0dd915af89e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-760022a2-75fb-5225-a136-0dd915af89e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-760022a2-75fb-5225-a136-0dd915af89e1" :answer/id #uuid "760022a2-75fb-5225-a136-0dd915af89e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{125}(x-3)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f867e6a6-dbb2-59f4-99c3-23f6d9793b91" :question/id #uuid "f867e6a6-dbb2-59f4-99c3-23f6d9793b91" :question/math-academy-id "q-148737" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=4\\sqrt[3]{x}-7.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=4\\sqrt[3]{x}-7\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=4\\sqrt[3]{y}-7.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\sqrt[3]{y}-7 \\\\ 4\\sqrt[3]{y} & =x+7 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =\\frac{1}{4}(x+7) \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{y})^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{4}(x+7))}^{3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{64}(x+7)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{64}(x+7)^{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1e400004-8c3b-55eb-9c62-48d0e98c825c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e400004-8c3b-55eb-9c62-48d0e98c825c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e400004-8c3b-55eb-9c62-48d0e98c825c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0f5a02a6-edc8-579d-9f3e-8685852c250f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41a67b62-1927-57c7-b8fd-09c8ea128d9c" "answer-2a68acc7-11c9-53ec-9edf-5225b6802e14" "answer-0f5a02a6-edc8-579d-9f3e-8685852c250f" "answer-b3dda357-db83-5268-bb16-701863b5d617" "answer-f16acb2b-4b5f-577f-b3ff-41c909981ff7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41a67b62-1927-57c7-b8fd-09c8ea128d9c" :answer/id #uuid "41a67b62-1927-57c7-b8fd-09c8ea128d9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=4(x+7)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a68acc7-11c9-53ec-9edf-5225b6802e14" :answer/id #uuid "2a68acc7-11c9-53ec-9edf-5225b6802e14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=64{x}^{3}+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f5a02a6-edc8-579d-9f3e-8685852c250f" :answer/id #uuid "0f5a02a6-edc8-579d-9f3e-8685852c250f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{64}(x+7)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3dda357-db83-5268-bb16-701863b5d617" :answer/id #uuid "b3dda357-db83-5268-bb16-701863b5d617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{7}(x+4)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f16acb2b-4b5f-577f-b3ff-41c909981ff7" :answer/id #uuid "f16acb2b-4b5f-577f-b3ff-41c909981ff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{7}{x}^{3}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-11b34dc5-01d5-59cc-afad-bce1d288e367" :question/id #uuid "11b34dc5-01d5-59cc-afad-bce1d288e367" :question/math-academy-id "q-148431" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}-4.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{x}-4\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt[3]{y}-4.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt[3]{y}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =x+4 \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{y})^{3} & =(x+4)^{3} \\\\ y & =(x+4)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=(x+4)^{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b24942f2-dc2d-5709-9d5c-fc4d35113cac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b24942f2-dc2d-5709-9d5c-fc4d35113cac" :answer-field/id #uuid "b24942f2-dc2d-5709-9d5c-fc4d35113cac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8bca345f-39c9-5521-bcba-a7055750252e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1547820e-1c6e-5874-a693-dbe63b833497" "answer-8bca345f-39c9-5521-bcba-a7055750252e" "answer-3cab048d-9187-5ff9-8179-12253f7ec205" "answer-f1b611fe-9f99-5df6-87f7-dbc5e83677ac" "answer-eb79fd11-c42f-5ea1-80c3-eeb2d1329843"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1547820e-1c6e-5874-a693-dbe63b833497" :answer/id #uuid "1547820e-1c6e-5874-a693-dbe63b833497" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=(x+2)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bca345f-39c9-5521-bcba-a7055750252e" :answer/id #uuid "8bca345f-39c9-5521-bcba-a7055750252e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=(x+4)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cab048d-9187-5ff9-8179-12253f7ec205" :answer/id #uuid "3cab048d-9187-5ff9-8179-12253f7ec205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=4{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1b611fe-9f99-5df6-87f7-dbc5e83677ac" :answer/id #uuid "f1b611fe-9f99-5df6-87f7-dbc5e83677ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)={x}^{3}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb79fd11-c42f-5ea1-80c3-eeb2d1329843" :answer/id #uuid "eb79fd11-c42f-5ea1-80c3-eeb2d1329843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)={x}^{3}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aa587d06-3d76-54dc-bc14-c7a25e414d3a" :question/id #uuid "aa587d06-3d76-54dc-bc14-c7a25e414d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-277045" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=6-4\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=6-4\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=6-4\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6-4\\sqrt{y} \\\\ 4\\sqrt{y} & =6-x \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & =\\frac{1}{4}(6-x) \\\\ (\\sqrt{y})^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{4}(6-x))}^{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{16}(6-x)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{16}(6-x)^{2}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx\\ge 0,\\,f(x)\\le 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx\\le 6,\\,{f}^{-1}(x)\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c7ff35a3-b189-5c5b-b194-1dd1bc180b94"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c7ff35a3-b189-5c5b-b194-1dd1bc180b94" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ff35a3-b189-5c5b-b194-1dd1bc180b94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-70556f37-c5ed-583c-a04b-123cc8508968" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70556f37-c5ed-583c-a04b-123cc8508968"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70556f37-c5ed-583c-a04b-123cc8508968" :answer/id #uuid "70556f37-c5ed-583c-a04b-123cc8508968" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-6)^2}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193001 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}-1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}-1\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}-1.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}-1 \\\\ x+1 & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x+1} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & =\\frac{3}{x+1} \\\\ (\\sqrt{y})^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{x+1})}^{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{(x+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{9}{(x+1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are given by\n\n$$\nx>0,\\,f(x)>-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx>-1,\\,{f}^{-1}(x)>0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186189892 :answer-field/correct "answer-a685ea85-b22a-51d2-9d33-2ac79331c9a6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f64ff466-0bca-57e1-8856-2a4a8172d8c4" "answer-b704f50d-5c35-5b3e-a0c8-af0ac5fd5317" "answer-94ffbd69-746d-5e22-8c95-44e785cd24cf" "answer-a685ea85-b22a-51d2-9d33-2ac79331c9a6" "answer-00fd4c22-89d2-5fde-b119-9ce2163bb9d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f64ff466-0bca-57e1-8856-2a4a8172d8c4" :answer/id #uuid "f64ff466-0bca-57e1-8856-2a4a8172d8c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=9(x+1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b704f50d-5c35-5b3e-a0c8-af0ac5fd5317" :answer/id #uuid "b704f50d-5c35-5b3e-a0c8-af0ac5fd5317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=9{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94ffbd69-746d-5e22-8c95-44e785cd24cf" :answer/id #uuid "94ffbd69-746d-5e22-8c95-44e785cd24cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{9}(x+1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a685ea85-b22a-51d2-9d33-2ac79331c9a6" :answer/id #uuid "a685ea85-b22a-51d2-9d33-2ac79331c9a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{9}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00fd4c22-89d2-5fde-b119-9ce2163bb9d1" :answer/id #uuid "00fd4c22-89d2-5fde-b119-9ce2163bb9d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{9}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f93430f2-f761-5264-8e7c-28207f8a2873" :question/id #uuid "f93430f2-f761-5264-8e7c-28207f8a2873" :question/math-academy-id "q-277064" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{x}}+1.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{x}}+1\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{y}}+1.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{y}}+1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{y}} & =x-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & =\\frac{2}{5(x-1)} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{y})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{2}{5(x-1)})}^{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{25(x-1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4}{25(x-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx>0,\\,f(x)>1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx>1,\\,{f}^{-1}(x)>0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2d41407-a63e-565f-bff1-4c6f38bb78e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2d41407-a63e-565f-bff1-4c6f38bb78e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2d41407-a63e-565f-bff1-4c6f38bb78e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-13479a97-4e44-5471-9c23-134ec902cd16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13479a97-4e44-5471-9c23-134ec902cd16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13479a97-4e44-5471-9c23-134ec902cd16" :answer/id #uuid "13479a97-4e44-5471-9c23-134ec902cd16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25(x-1)^2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193013 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=3-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=3-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=3-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[3]{y}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[3]{y}} \\\\ x-3 & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[3]{y}} \\\\ 3-x & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt[3]{y}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3-x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =\\frac{4}{3-x} \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{y})^{3} & ={(\\frac{4}{3-x})}^{3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{64}{(3-x)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{64}{(3-x)^{3}}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: The domain and range of $f(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx\\ne 0,\\,f(x)\\ne 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain and range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx\\ne 3,\\,{f}^{-1}(x)\\ne 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186189964 :answer-field/correct "answer-fbf8be41-e92b-561f-ad73-49d08a3c31d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7b2900c9-1a52-5c45-aed2-605280ab5a10" "answer-8aaf